      "description": "Text action with extended pointer target.",
      "html": "<button type=\"button\" class=\"ds-link\">Inspect the source observations</button>",
      "css": ".ds-link{font-family:var(--font,\"Host Grotesk\",ui-sans-serif,sans-serif);position:relative;padding:0;border:0;background:none;color:var(--blue,#d5f96e);font-size:12px;font-weight:500;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:4px;cursor:pointer;transition:transform 160ms}.ds-link::after{content:\"\";position:absolute;left:0;right:0;top:50%;height:44px;transform:translateY(-50%)}.ds-link:hover{background:none}.ds-link:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--blue,#d5f96e);outline-offset:3px;}.ds-link:active:not(:disabled){transform:translateY(1px)}.ds-link:disabled{cursor:not-allowed;opacity:.55}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-link{transition:none}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Evidence field",
      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "evidence-input",
      "description": "A visible prompt, hint and resizable notebook field.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-field\"><label for=\"ds-claim\">What’s your claim?</label><span id=\"ds-claim-hint\">What do the observations support?</span><textarea id=\"ds-claim\" aria-describedby=\"ds-claim-hint\" rows=\"3\" placeholder=\"I think these observations…\"></textarea></div>",
      "css": ".ds-field{font-family:var(--font,\"Host Grotesk\",ui-sans-serif,sans-serif);color:var(--ink,#f5f6f7)}.ds-field label{display:block;font-size:13px;font-weight:500}.ds-field span{display:block;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted,#a6acb2);margin:4px 0 8px}.ds-field textarea{font-family:var(--font,\"Host Grotesk\",ui-sans-serif,sans-serif);display:block;width:100%;min-height:88px;resize:vertical;padding:12px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong,#50565c);border-radius:var(--radius-sm,10px);background:var(--field-bg,#0c0f10);color:var(--ink,#f5f6f7);font-size:14px;line-height:1.6}.ds-field textarea::placeholder{color:var(--placeholder,#9aa1aa)}.ds-field textarea:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--blue,#d5f96e);outline-offset:3px;}@media(max-width:560px){.ds-field textarea{font-size:16px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Navigation",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "navigation",
      "description": "Muted navigation with a graphite evidence destination.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-nav\" aria-label=\"Main\"><a href=\"#investigations\" aria-current=\"page\">Investigations</a><a href=\"#query\">Search coordinates</a><a href=\"#my-evidence\">My evidence</a></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-nav{font-family:var(--font,\"Host Grotesk\",ui-sans-serif,sans-serif);display:flex;gap:8px;background:var(--paper,#08090a)}.ds-nav a{display:flex;align-items:center;min-height:44px;padding:8px 16px;border-radius:999px;font-size:13px;font-weight:450;color:var(--muted,#a6acb2);text-decoration:none}.ds-nav a:hover{color:var(--ink,#f5f6f7);background:var(--surface,#121416)}.ds-nav a[aria-current=page]{background:transparent;color:var(--ink,#f5f6f7)}.ds-nav a:last-child{background:#1b1e20;color:#e5e8eb;padding-inline:20px}.ds-nav a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--blue,#d5f96e);outline-offset:3px;}@media(max-width:560px){.ds-nav{gap:0}.ds-nav a{padding:8px 10px;font-size:12px}.ds-nav a:first-child{display:none}.ds-nav a:last-child{padding-inline:12px}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Quality status",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "quality-flagged",
      "description": "Written status retains the meaning of its color.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-quality\" data-status=\"flagged\">Flagged near target</span>",
      "css": ".ds-quality{font-family:var(--font,\"Host Grotesk\",ui-sans-serif,sans-serif);display:inline-block;font-size:12px;font-weight:500;padding:4px 7px;border-radius:var(--radius-xs,6px);white-space:nowrap}.ds-quality[data-status=flagged]{background:var(--amber-bg,#33291b);color:var(--amber-ink,#f3cc8d)}.ds-quality[data-status=clear]{background:var(--lime,#24301e);color:var(--green,#c7e5aa)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Evidence notebook",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "notebook",
      "description": "Cool graphite distinguishes reasoning from the image bench.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-notebook\"><header><p>Make your reasoning visible</p><h2>Evidence notebook</h2></header><div class=\"ds-notebook-body\">A useful answer includes what you saw and what you still can’t tell.</div></section>",
      "css": ".ds-notebook{font-family:var(--font,\"Host Grotesk\",ui-sans-serif,sans-serif);color:var(--ink,#f5f6f7);background:var(--surface,#121416);border:1px solid var(--lavender-line,#313c40);border-radius:var(--radius-lg,24px);overflow:hidden}.ds-notebook header{padding:22px 20px;background:var(--lavender,#14191b);border-bottom:1px solid var(--lavender-line,#313c40)}.ds-notebook header p{margin:0 0 4px;color:var(--lavender-eyebrow,#a3b8c0);text-transform:uppercase;font-size:12px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:.06em;line-height:1.5}.ds-notebook h2{margin:0;font-size:21px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-.02em;line-height:1.3}.ds-notebook-body{padding:20px;color:var(--muted,#a6acb2);font-size:12px;line-height:1.6}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Comparison selector",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "comparison-selected",
      "description": "Pressed state identifies the selected scientific pair.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-pair\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Choose comparison\"><button type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"true\">A + B<span>Different dates</span></button><button type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">A + C<span>Different wavelengths</span></button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-pair{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:3px;border:1px solid var(--line,#2a2d30);border-radius:12px;background:var(--paper,#08090a)}.ds-pair button{font-family:var(--font,\"Host Grotesk\",ui-sans-serif,sans-serif);min-height:44px;padding:9px 13px;border:1px solid var(--line,#2a2d30);border-radius:var(--radius-sm,10px);font-size:14px;font-weight:500;cursor:pointer;transition:background 160ms,color 160ms,border-color 160ms,transform 160ms;min-height:45px;padding:6px 13px;background:transparent;border-color:transparent;text-align:left;font-size:12px;line-height:1.25;color:var(--ink,#f5f6f7)}.ds-pair button span{display:block;font-size:12px;font-weight:400;margin-top:3px;color:var(--muted,#a6acb2)}.ds-pair button[aria-pressed=true]{background:var(--cornflower,#222a18);border-color:var(--cornflower-line,#62723d);color:var(--blue-deep,#c3e75e)}.ds-pair button:hover:not(:disabled){border-color:var(--blue-hover-line,#a5bb6d)}.ds-pair button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--blue,#d5f96e);outline-offset:3px;}.ds-pair button:active:not(:disabled){transform:translateY(1px)}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-pair button{transition:none}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Orbit mark",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "brand-mark",
      "description": "Exact inline geometry from BrandMark.tsx; decorative within a named brand link.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-brand\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 40 40\" fill=\"none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><ellipse cx=\"20\" cy=\"20\" rx=\"18\" ry=\"10\" transform=\"rotate(-34 20 20)\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"20\" r=\"7\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><circle cx=\"33.5\" cy=\"10.8\" r=\"3.1\" class=\"ds-orbit-point\"/></svg>perigee</span>",
      "css": ".ds-brand{font-family:var(--font,\"Host Grotesk\",ui-sans-serif,sans-serif);display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;color:var(--ink,#f5f6f7);font-size:26px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.035em;line-height:1}.ds-brand svg{display:block;width:34px;height:34px}.ds-orbit-point{fill:var(--blue,#d5f96e);stroke:var(--paper,#08090a);stroke-width:1.5}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Orbital Observatory",
    "overview": "A black sky, white typography and electric citron invite a learner into an investigation. The existing orbit mark is refined into a tilted ellipse, central ring and small orbital point. Host Grotesk connects the expansive, centered landing introduction to the quieter graphite workbench.\n\nThe landing surface uses decorative white stars and generous reading space. Working views concentrate on registered scientific images, nearby metadata and a reusable evidence notebook. This record describes the current React application, including its API and clearly labeled fixture modes; it does not describe the superseded light prototype or certify a deployment.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Black and white identity with electric citron actions and selection.",
      "Self-hosted Host Grotesk with a large landing display and compact working hierarchy.",
      "Rounded graphite containers, image-led investigations and persistent evidence context.",
      "Decorative orbital motion on the landing page; deliberate user-controlled scientific playback in the bench."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Scientific Color Rule",
        "body": "Keep quality states, coverage hatching, prediction markers and the guide visually distinct; the brand accent must not change what a scientific overlay means.",
        "section": "colors"
